{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CduVES8bkzpjeZSZRofZY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Weekly REVIEW complete. `reports/decision_review/REVIEW_2026-08-11.md` written; `REVIEW_TODO.md` updated (19 items carried, 4 new appended).\n\n**Gate check**: `event_index_latest.json` `generated_at = 2026-08-11T01:35:28` — today, so no abort.\n\n**The controlling fact this week**: the previous REVIEW was only 2 days ago (08-09). All 5 new deep-dives sit at 3–6% window completion, so the `win100 decided` set diffs to **added 0 / removed 0** — 152 rows, identical members. Rec 7's gap (10.8pp), all three Rec 11 metrics, and TODO-013's dispersion split came back bit-for-bit identical. I recorded them as `no_change (re-measurement)` and explicitly did **not** advance the \"consecutive weeks\" counters — mechanically accumulating would have tripped Rec 7 into `paused` on a re-read of the same sample. That is TODO-024's exact failure mode, now with a concrete instance.\n\n**Genuinely new findings** (all from the authoritative data layer, not new samples):\n\n1. **Rec 4's root cause is misdiagnosed** — it's a join gap, not a parser gap. All 7 `macro_delta` nulls are recoverable from `news/news_logs/<date>_digest.json` (08-06 = −0.1, 08-07 = −0.75, 08-10 = +0.3). A further 5 rows have *scraped values that disagree with authoritative* (04-14: −0.3 vs −1.2). 12/74 = 16.2% wrong-or-missing. Two corollaries: the long-standing \"2026-04-15 is legit v1 n/a\" belief is refuted (authoritative 0.0), and TODO-011's \"upstream stopped producing strong signals\" is wrong — upstream produced 2 more (06-24 −0.70, 08-07 −0.75); they were lost at the join.\n\n2. **Same structural defect, two independent sources.** `build_event_index.py` opens no authoritative JSON at all — deep-dive hot-zone (0/175 in index vs 18 in `history.json`, 6/15 shadow mismatches, non-trivial states 4/4 wrong) and news-digest `macro_delta` are the same failure: the extractor reads the presentation layer. The news header change on 08-06 is what made it visible.\n\n3. **`decision_id` is not unique** — 456 rows, 452 unique. `thematic-screener_2026-07-30` appears twice with *opposite* verdicts (miss vs hit). Since `diff_verdict_flips.py` keys on it, this week's 13.8% flip rate rests on a defective key, so TODO-010 should not close yet.\n\n4. **Pattern F (new, med confidence)**: within Semiconductors, active-stance miss is 14.3% (4/28) vs conservative 65.6% (21/32) — a 51.3pp split. The signal may be stance × score-band rather than industry, which is the axis Rec 11's exception is currently keyed on.\n\nI proposed **no protocol-layer changes** — both preconditions fail (zero sample growth; authoritative join not landed, so hot-zone evidence still rests on 40%-error shadow values). Recommended priority: TODO-020 + 025 + 026 as one `build_event_index.py` data-layer PR.\n\nOne caveat on scope: I read `event_index_latest.json` structurally via Python rather than as raw text — at 2.3MB it exceeds what a direct Read returns, and the per-field queries above cover the full 456 rows."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1105,"cache_read_input_tokens":168225,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1105},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"573d0e1f-dd1d-4dd9-88c8-3ffe589561e4","uuid":"aaa1b090-235b-4bb1-b7b3-090f986c2ac8","timestamp":"2026-08-10T17:47:54.986Z","request_id":"req_011CduVEQwQrFyyUB6gubS5K"}
